title: Political communication and party competition in the Federal Republic of Germany (BA Political Science)
description: "The introductory course deals with political communication and party competition in the Federal Republic of Germany. The learning objectives are (1) to introduce theories, concepts, and methods from the field of political communication, and (2) to examine their relevance for party competition in the Federal Republic of Germany. Among other things, the course addresses the positions of political parties, populist communication, and the transformation of election campaign communication through social media in Germany. Note: course taught in German."
instructor: Christoph Ivanusch
